\section{What is mapped}{

By default the posterior \code{statistic} of the \strong{expected response} (see
\code{\link[=predict.bm_fit]{predict.bm_fit()}}). With \code{uncertainty = "width"} (or \code{TRUE}) the map shows the
credible-interval width (\code{upper - lower}), with \code{"sd"} the posterior standard
deviation, and with \code{"alpha"} the statistic is drawn with transparency that
increases with the interval width. The uncertainty of a map of expected
responses reflects parameter (and simulated random-effect) uncertainty, not
observation noise; use \code{type = "predictive"} predictions for prediction
intervals.
